   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "79d69b6f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part 2 · Synthetic Data Generation for *Solea senegalensis*\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is the second part of the *Beyond the Scale* series, which asks whether synthetic data can help address the small-dataset problem in aquaculture AI. It fits three SDV synthesisers on the real training set, evaluates how faithfully they reproduce the biological and statistical structure of the real fish, and runs a first predictive benchmark.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notebook:** `part2_synthetic_generation.ipynb`  \n",
    "**Requires:** `data/processed/real_train.parquet`, created in `part1_eda_v2.ipynb`  \n",
    "**Never loads:** `data/processed/real_test.parquet`, which stays sealed until Part 3\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Fit three SDV synthesisers (GaussianCopula, CTGAN, TVAE) on the real training set.\n",
    "2. Generate five independent replicas at four augmentation proportions (25 %, 50 %, 100 %, 200 %).\n",
    "3. Apply biological validity filters and compute pass rates.\n",
    "4. Evaluate univariate fidelity, multivariate fidelity and allometric preservation.\n",
    "5. Compute a preliminary TSTR benchmark (train on synthetic, test on real, via cross-validation).\n",
    "6. Save all synthetic datasets and the accompanying manifest for Part 3.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Methodological contract:** the real test set is never loaded, inspected or referenced anywhere in this notebook. It remains sealed for the final evaluation in Part 3."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d5d09f15",
